  📌 Exemplo 1: Admin fazendo login

  1. Admin faz login → Recebe JWT token
           ↓
  2. Frontend chama GET /api/sidebar
     (com Bearer token)
           ↓
  3. Backend valida token → Identifica user
           ↓
  4. Backend busca:
     - user.role_id = '[admin_role_id]'
           ↓
  5. Backend busca permissions do role:
     SELECT p.* FROM user_permissions p
     JOIN role_permissions rp ON rp.permission_id = p.id
     WHERE rp.role_id = '[admin_role_id]'

     Retorna: ['users.list', 'users.view', 'users.create',
               'users.update', 'users.delete', 'users.reset_password']
           ↓
  6. Backend busca routes vinculadas às permissions:
     SELECT r.* FROM sidebar_routes r
     JOIN user_permissions p ON p.route_id = r.id
     WHERE p.name IN ('users.list', 'users.view', ...)
           ↓
  7. Backend busca submenus dessas routes:
     SELECT s.* FROM sidebar_submenus s
     WHERE s.id IN (SELECT route.submenu_id FROM routes)
           ↓
  8. Backend busca menus desses submenus:
     SELECT m.* FROM sidebar_menus m
     WHERE m.id IN (SELECT submenu.menu_id FROM submenus)
           ↓
